.TH "WWALD" "1" "2026-10-30" "wwal 1.2.0" "WayWal Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
wwald - zero-copy Wayland wallpaper, VA-API video, Shadertoy, and Material You daemon
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBwwald\fR [OPTIONS]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBwwald\fR is the background rendering daemon for \fBwwal\fR(1). Written in ISO C23 with a stripped binary size under 1.4 MB, \fBwwald\fR replaces separate static wallpaper daemons, video wallpaper players, GLSL shader backgrounds, Steam Wallpaper Engine runners, and color scheme / template generators within a single sandboxed process.
.PP
When invoked via a symlink named \fBswww-daemon\fR or \fBawww-daemon\fR, \fBwwald\fR automatically enables full \fBswww\fR / \fBawww\fR v0.12.1 daemon flag and socket namespace compatibility.
.PP
.SH ARCHITECTURE
.PP
.SS Event Loop & Systemd Socket Activation
.PP
\fBwwald\fR drives all Wayland protocol events, IPC client connections, \fBtimerfd\fR frame clocks, \fBsignalfd\fR, and compositor occlusion sockets through a Linux \fBio_uring\fR(7) event loop using multishot poll (\fBIORING_POLL_ADD_MULTI\fR), with an automatic \fBepoll\fR(7) fallback on older kernels.
.PP
When started via \fBsystemd\fR(1) socket activation (\fBwwald.socket\fR), \fBwwald\fR inherits the listening socket from \fBSD_LISTEN_FDS\fR (\fBLISTEN_FDS\fR / \fBLISTEN_PID\fR, file descriptor 3) at \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wwald.sock\fR and skips \fBunlink\fR(2) on shutdown so the socket unit remains reusable across restarts. When started standalone, it binds \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/$WAYLAND_DISPLAY-wwald.<namespace>.sock\fR (or \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/wwald.sock\fR).
.PP
.SS Zero-Copy DMA-BUF & HiDPI Rendering Pipeline
.PP
\fBwwald\fR negotiates hardware scanout formats and DRM format modifiers directly with the Wayland compositor via \fBzwp_linux_dmabuf_feedback_v1\fR:
.IP \(bu 2
Matches the compositor's exact primary DRM device (\fBdev_t\fR) and per-surface scanout tranches across single-GPU and hybrid iGPU+dGPU systems.
.IP \(bu 2
Allocates GBM buffer objects using optimal vendor-tiled or compressed modifiers (NVIDIA Block-Linear, AMD DCC, Intel CCS, ARM AFBC) when GPU compute is active, or \fBDRM_FORMAT_MOD_LINEAR\fR for CPU SIMD fallback (\fBAVX-512\fR, \fBAVX2\fR, \fBARM NEON\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
Supports true 10-bit HDR10 wide-gamut surfaces (\fBDRM_FORMAT_XRGB2101010\fR / \fBDRM_FORMAT_ARGB2101010\fR), zero-RAM solid colors via \fBwp_single_pixel_buffer_v1\fR, and explicit GPU fence synchronization via \fBwp_linux_drm_syncobj_v1\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Separates physical pixel dimensions from logical surface dimensions using \fBwp_fractional_scale_v1\fR and \fBwp_viewporter\fR, guaranteeing crisp 1:1 physical pixel rendering on fractionally scaled 4K/5K displays.
.PP
.SS Zero-FFmpeg Hardware Video Engine
.PP
\fBwwald\fR contains a native, zero-allocation MP4 (\fBisobmff\fR) and WebM/Matroska (\fBEBML\fR) demuxer coupled directly to \fBlibva\fR (\fBVA-API\fR):
.IP \(bu 2
Parses H.264 (SPS/PPS/VUI/Slice/DPB), HEVC (VPS/SPS/PPS/RPS), VP9, and AV1 bitstreams in-process without linking \fBlibavformat\fR or \fBlibavcodec\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Evicts already-played file pages from the Linux page cache via \fBmadvise\fR(2) \fBMADV_DONTNEED\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
On AMD (\fBradeonsi\fR) and Intel (\fBiHD\fR) GPUs, exports decoded \fBDRM_FORMAT_NV12\fR and \fBDRM_FORMAT_P010\fR surfaces via \fBVA_EXPORT_SURFACE_COMPOSED_LAYERS\fR for direct zero-VPP KMS hardware overlay plane scanout.
.IP \(bu 2
On NVIDIA GPUs (\fBlibva-nvidia-driver\fR), exports separate layers into a compact 3-surface VA-API Video Post-Processing (VPP) \fBBGRX\fR ring.
.IP \(bu 2
Synchronizes frame presentation to display VBlank using a Phase-Locked Loop (PLL) fed by \fBwp_presentation_feedback\fR timestamps.
.PP
.SS Native Wallpaper Engine, Multi-Pass Shadertoy & Reactive Audio/MPRIS2
.PP
\fBwwald\fR includes a native Wallpaper Engine (\fB431960\fR) Workshop runtime, a multi-pass Shadertoy pipeline, 10 built-in procedural shader presets, and reactive desktop bridges:
.IP \(bu 2
Maps \fBPKGV0001..PKGV0022\fR \fBscene.pkg\fR archives directly via \fBmmap\fR(2) without temporary disk extraction, decoding \fBTEXV0005\fR (\fBBC1\fR, \fBBC2\fR, \fBBC3\fR, \fBBC7\fR, and \fBLZ4\fR) textures, 2D Puppet Warp (\fB.mdl\fR) skeletal meshes, 32-byte-aligned AVX2 Structure-of-Arrays particle systems, `"sound"` ambient audio layers, `"text"` clock/label layers, and sandboxed \fBSceneScript\fR logic.
.IP \(bu 2
Executes multi-pass Shadertoy fragment shaders (\fBBuffer A\fR..\fBBuffer D\fR \fBGL_RGBA16F\fR ping-pong passes, \fBiChannel0\fR..\fBiChannel3\fR, \fB#pragma waywal\fR, hardware derivatives), 10 built-in procedural shader presets, and 2.5D Depth-Map Parallax Occlusion Mapping driven by cursor and workspace-slide spring physics.
.IP \(bu 2
Streams lock-free PipeWire 2048-point AVX2 64-bin Bark-scale FFT spectrum data, automatically ducks wallpaper audio when external media plays, and listens to D-Bus \fBMPRIS2\fR signals with zero idle polling to expose \fBu_album_art\fR, \fBu_media_playing\fR, and live album art Material Design 3 palettes.
.PP
.SS Zero-Watt Smart Occlusion & Battery Governor
.PP
\fBwwald\fR maintains a per-output pause bitmask (\fBwaywal_pause_reason_t\fR):
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWAYWAL_PAUSE_DPMS_OR_UNMAPPED\fR (\fB1 << 0\fR): Output is unmapped or in DPMS sleep.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWAYWAL_PAUSE_TOPLEVEL_FULLSCREEN\fR (\fB1 << 1\fR): Fullscreen window covers the output (tracked via \fBzwlr_foreign_toplevel_manager_v1\fR, \fBext_foreign_toplevel_list_v1\fR, or Hyprland/Sway IPC sockets).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWAYWAL_PAUSE_TOPLEVEL_MAXIMIZED\fR (\fB1 << 2\fR): Maximized window covers the output.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWAYWAL_PAUSE_WORKSPACE_OCCLUDED\fR (\fB1 << 3\fR): Active workspace on the output is fully tiled/opaque.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWAYWAL_PAUSE_SESSION_IDLE\fR (\fB1 << 4\fR): Session idle notification received via \fBext_idle_notifier_v1\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWAYWAL_PAUSE_BATTERY_SAVER\fR (\fB1 << 5\fR): Laptop battery discharging or power-saver profile active (monitored via \fBinotify\fR on \fB/sys/class/power_supply/\fR).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBWAYWAL_PAUSE_USER_MANUAL\fR (\fB1 << 6\fR): Paused explicitly via \fBwwal pause\fR.
.PP
Whenever all active outputs have a non-zero \fBpause_mask\fR, \fBwwald\fR disarms its frame \fBtimerfd\fR, dropping CPU, GPU, and NVDEC utilization to strictly \fB0.00%\fR (\fB0 wakeups/sec\fR).
.PP
.SS Landlock & Seccomp-BPF Sandboxing
.PP
At startup, after initializing DRM/GBM and Wayland connections, \fBwwald\fR locks itself down using:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBPR_SET_NO_NEW_PRIVS\fR and \fBPR_SET_DUMPABLE = 0\fR.
.IP \(bu 2
Linux \fBLandlock\fR (\fBABI v1..v4\fR): Restricts filesystem visibility to read-only system libraries, device nodes, \fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR, and configured wallpaper/cache/template directories, blocking access to sensitive user data (\fB~/.ssh\fR, \fB~/.gnupg\fR, etc.).
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSeccomp-BPF\fR syscall allowlist: Blocks network socket creation (\fBAF_INET\fR, \fBAF_INET6\fR), \fBptrace\fR, and privilege escalation syscalls.
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB-n, --namespace\fR <NAME>
.RS 4
Set the IPC socket and Wayland layer-shell namespace (default: \fBdefault\fR, or \fB$SWWW_NAMESPACE\fR / \fB$AWWW_NAMESPACE\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB-d, --daemon\fR
.RS 4
Fork into the background and signal readiness once the IPC socket and Wayland surfaces are initialized.
.RE
.PP
\fB--no-daemon\fR
.RS 4
Stay in the foreground (\fBswww-daemon\fR / \fBawww-daemon\fR compatibility).
.RE
.PP
\fB-f, --format\fR <xrgb|xbgr|rgb|bgr>
.RS 4
Pixel channel order hint (\fBswww-daemon\fR / \fBawww-daemon\fR compatibility).
.RE
.PP
\fB-q, --quiet\fR
.RS 4
Suppress informational log messages.
.RE
.PP
\fB--layer\fR <background|bottom>
.RS 4
Set default Wayland layer-shell placement (default: \fBbackground\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--backdrop\fR <none|auto-blur|PATH>
.RS 4
Configure secondary overview backdrop layer surface mode (default: \fBnone\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--battery-policy\fR <ignore|reduce-fps|pause-video>
.RS 4
Set laptop battery power governance policy (default: \fBreduce-fps\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--volume\fR <0.0..1.0>
.RS 4
Set default wallpaper audio playback volume (default: \fB0.0\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fB--mute-on-audio\fR, \fB--no-mute-on-audio\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable automatic PipeWire volume ducking when external audio plays.
.RE
.PP
\fB--theme-from-media\fR, \fB--no-theme-from-media\fR
.RS 4
Enable or disable dynamic Material Design 3 palette extraction from D-Bus MPRIS2 album art.
.RE
.PP
\fB-v, --verbose\fR
.RS 4
Enable verbose logging.
.RE
.PP
\fB-V, --version\fR
.RS 4
Print version information and exit.
.RE
.PP
\fB-h, --help\fR
.RS 4
Display help message and exit.
.RE
.PP
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBWWAL_CONFIG_PATH\fR
.RS 4
Explicit path to \fBconfig.toml\fR (defaults to \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/wwal/config.toml\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBWWAL_WORKSHOP_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Override Steam Workshop (\fB431960\fR) directory path.
.RE
.PP
\fBWWAL_WE_ASSETS_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Override Wallpaper Engine default assets directory path.
.RE
.PP
\fBWWAL_SHADER_PRESET_DIR\fR, \fBWWAL_SHADER_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Override directory searched for shader presets (\fB.glsl\fR, \fB.frag\fR) before falling back to embedded procedural shaders.
.RE
.PP
\fBWWAL_CACHE_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Override cache directory path (defaults to \fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME/wwal\fR and \fB$XDG_CACHE_HOME/wal\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBWWAL_STATE_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Override persistent state directory path (defaults to \fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/wwal\fR).
.RE
.PP
\fBSWWW_NAMESPACE\fR, \fBAWWW_NAMESPACE\fR
.RS 4
Fallback socket namespace when \fB-n\fR is not specified.
.RE
.PP
.SH SIGNALS
.PP
\fBSIGTERM\fR, \fBSIGINT\fR
.RS 4
Gracefully tear down Wayland surfaces, release GBM/VA-API buffers, and exit.
.RE
.PP
\fBSIGHUP\fR
.RS 4
Reload \fB~/.config/wwal/config.toml\fR and re-evaluate active solar/schedule rules and templates.
.RE
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
